Cassandra Database (Docker Desktop)
Steps:
1.Open Docker Desktop > Terminal > Enable
2.docker pull Cassandra
3.docker --version
4.docker run --name ak-cassandra-db -d -p 9042:9042 cassandra:4.1
5.docker ps [process]
6.docker logs -f ak-cassandra-db [ctrl+c to exit]
7.To Client (cqlsh)
8.docker exec -it ak-cassandra-db cqlsh

Practical No. 01:

1} Create a database student with 5 records 
2} Display all the records
3} Select record with id=112
4} Display records with course CS

Step 1 — Create the keyspace

CREATE KEYSPACE student WITH replication = {
'class': 'SimpleStrategy', 'replication_factor': 1
};

Then: USE student;

Step 2 — Create the table

CREATE TABLE students ( id int PRIMARY KEY, name text,
course text
);

Step 3 — Insert 5 records

INSERT INTO students (id, name, course) VALUES (111, 'Amit', 'IT');

INSERT INTO students (id, name, course) VALUES (112, 'Rahul', 'CS');

INSERT INTO students (id, name, course) VALUES (113, 'Priya', 'DS');

INSERT INTO students (id, name, course) VALUES (114, 'Sneha', 'CS');

INSERT INTO students (id, name, course) VALUES (115, 'Ravi', 'IT');

Step 4 — Display all students

SELECT * FROM students;

Step 5 — Display student with ID 112

SELECT * FROM students WHERE id = 112;

Step 6 — Display students from CS

SELECT * FROM students WHERE course = 'CS' ALLOW FILTERING;
